language Essence 1.3

$ Scaling guard for set (representation explicit) over a large inner domain.
$
$ A fixed-cardinality explicit set needs two slots regardless of how big the inner domain is, so
$ both the model and the rewrite must stay the same size as int(1..n) grows. Rule-attempt counts in
$ stats.toml are the guard: they must not start scaling with the inner-domain size.

find i : int(1..100)
find s : set (representation explicit, size 2) of int(1..10000)

such that i in s, |s| = 2
